    <statement><p>State the domain and range of each of the following functions:</p>
<p>(Enter your answers as inequalities: .
Your domains should be inequalities in <m>x</m> and ranges, in <m>y</m>.
As always, type <em> pi </em> for <m>\pi</m>.
If you wish to enter <m>\infty</m>, type <em>infinity</em>.)</p>
<p>(a) <m>f(x) = \arccos{(x)}</m> has</p>
<p>Domain: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Range: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(b) <m>g(x) = \arcsin{(x)}</m> has</p>
<p>Domain: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>Range: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>(c) <m>h(x) = \arctan{(x)}</m> has</p>
<p>Domain: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>Range: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1\le x\le 1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0\le y\le \pi </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1\le x\le 1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-\pi }{2}\le y\le \frac{\pi }{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-\infty  &lt; x &lt; \infty </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-\pi }{2} &lt; y &lt; \frac{\pi }{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



(a) The domain of <m>f</m> is <m>-1 \le x \le 1</m>, so <m>\arccos{(x)}</m> is
defined only if <m>x</m> is between <m>-1</m> and <m>1</m> inclusive.
The range is between <m>0</m> and <m>\pi</m> inclusive.



(b) The domain of <m>g</m> is <m>-1 \le x \le 1</m>, so <m>\arcsin{(x)}</m> is
defined only if <m>x</m> is between <m>-1</m> and <m>1</m> inclusive.
The range is between <m>-\frac{\pi}{2}</m> and <m>\frac{\pi}{2}</m> inclusive.



(c) The domain of <m>h</m> is all real numbers, so <m>\arctan{(x)}</m> is
defined for all values of <m>x</m>.
The range is between but not including <m>-\frac{\pi}{2}</m> and <m>\frac{\pi}{2}</m>.



</solution>
